{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Is HMTL a Programming Language?"}, {"type": "position", "content": 3}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A1.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use to compare markup languages with programming languages."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common simple incidents at work in a simple spoken or written situation with a supportive interlocutor. Assess the incident of data in the macrosystem processes, based on the data dictionary to consolidate intervening data, based in established parameters."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Communicates effectively in English about the communicative topics for this level through the use of appropriate basic vocabulary and grammatical structures, and with intelligible pronunciation.  Exchanges simple information on programming tools and solutions to a client's requirement."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple past Tense Statements with Frequency Adverbs"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use <span class=\"strong\">  simple past </span>  when you want to refer events that end in a specific moment in the past."}, {"type": "example", "content": "HTML was always considered a markup language."}, {"type": "text", "content": "When you use <span class=\"strong\">simple past</span>  you can use some <span class=\"strong\">adverbs of frequency</span> to say with what frequency you did the actions in the past. <br /><br />  The <span class= \"strong\"> adverbs</span> can be placed at the beginning of the sentence but are always after the verb <span class= \"strong\"> to be</span> . <br > Example: <br > <span class=\"italic\">They <span class= \"strong\">were never</span>  made with a markup language. </span>  <br> <br> But most of the time adverbs are placed before the main verb in a sentence. <br>Example: <br> <span class=\"italic\">I <span class= \"strong\">always used </span> HTML to create programs. </span> <br />"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":10,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">  FREQUENCY</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> <span class=\\\"strong\\\">  ADVERB</span> </div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">0%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Never</div> \\t\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">5%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Rarely</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">15%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Seldom</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">35%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Ocassionally</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">50%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Sometimes</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">60%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Frequently</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">70%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Normally</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">85%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Usually</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\">100%</div>\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"<div class=\\\"center_text\\\"> Always</div>\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\"\"}"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Types of Markup Language"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "There are three types of markup language."}, {"type": "text", "content": "The general categories of electronic markup are: <br /><br /><ul> <li> The type of markup called <span class= \"strong\"> presentational</span>  used by traditional word- processing systems or binary codes installed in a document text that creates an effect in which content can be seen while is being edited.<br /><br /> </li><li>\u2022\tThe type of markup called <span class= \"strong\"> procedural </span> is installed in text to provide instructions for text process programs. This kind of markup allows authors to edit the text visibly and directly. <br /><br /> </li><li> The <span class= \"strong\"> descriptive </span> markup is used to label document parts.  Some examples are HTML and XML. This markup encourages authors to write in a conceptually form not visually. <br /><br />"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "comparison"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the act of referring at two things to say the are similar"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: To make a programming language and markup language comparison, we first have to know perfectly what they are."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "direction"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "an act of telling a person or a thing what to do and how to do it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They are made to give directions to a computer. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "conduct"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the way a person or a thing behaves"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Designers created them to give directions to a computer, allowing the creation of programs, which can control the conduct of the machine."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "symbols"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a conventional sign used in writing"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: In markup languages you write document with symbols and words encapsulated by tags, replacing long sentences with short instructions in digital media."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "encapsulate"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to enclose between two things"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb) "}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: You write documents with symbols and words encapsulated by tags."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "capability"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the potential to do something "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: We can find some capabilities such as drag and drop, local storage or geolocation. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n2le02ob03aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Define with your own words Programming and Markup Languages."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Make a list of examples for each language."}, {"type": "text", "content": "Do you consider HTML a programming language? Why?"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Present your poster to your classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I can identify the characteristics of a Programming and a Markup Language."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can classify different system languages into Programming or Markup according to its function."}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can explain my opinion about HTML. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I can demonstrate my knowledge about system languages."}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"_data": [], "title": "", "type": "audio", "template_override": 1, "id": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"audiosrc": "enpe8n2le02ob03re2aud01", "images": [{"time": "0", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob03re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<div align=\"justify\"><span class=\"strong\"> Eric: </span> To make a programming language and markup language comparison, we first have to know perfectly what they are. <br>\nProgramming languages are different from markup languages because they are constructed languages divided into two components: the form and the meaning. Designers created them to give directions to a computer, allowing the creation of programs, which can control the conduct of the machine. These languages work through algorithms to write computer programs and even control computer external devices. Besides, they let humans communicate with machines.</div>"}, {"time": "37500", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob03re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">On the other hand, markup languages are systems, which present information without instructions. To do so, you write documents with symbols and words encapsulated by tags, replacing long sentences with short instructions in digital media.</div>"}, {"time": "55000", "image": "enpe8n2le02ob03re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<div align=\"justify\">People never thought of HTML as a programming language; programmers usually considered that HTML didn't have many capabilities. This is why designers always considered HTML a markup language and during some time that was true, and there are people who think that HTML has capabilities normally associated with the development language. We can find some capabilities such as drag and drop, local storage or geolocation. Programmers often created some famous applications entirely with HTML and a few CSS. Do developers say those are not enough reasons to consider HTML a programming language? Actually, they do. However, something real is that, nowadays, programmers use HTML for the creation of applications, and that is a good reason to consider it a programming language.</div>"}], "coverimg": "enpe8n2le02ob03re2img01.jpg"}, "type": "slideshow"}]}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about programming languages and markup languages. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can discuss the reasons to consider HTML a programming language."}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can list capabilities associated with a development language."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think applications have made people's life easier? Why?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "What are the websites you use the most? Why?"}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "content": {"attempt_feedback": [{"type": "text", "content": "You have 2 tries"}, {"type": "text", "content": "you have 1 attempt left"}], "co